<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.jkrumm.warden-poll</string>
  <!-- The ingest poller. Polls UptimeKuma, Docker (homelab + vps), GitHub,
       Slack #alerts/#updates, Hermes self-state, 1Password ref health, and
       stray agent-created skills; reconciles into the ledger and composes the
       NEW/RESOLVED digest.

       Was gateway cron job 4b1faabda97d ("Watchdog", */30, no_agent: true):
       the gateway invoked watchdog-slack.py, which loaded this module, called
       main(["--slack-body"]), and delivered the printed stdout to Slack channel
       C0ASRULFTSS itself. Promoting it removes the scheduling dependency on the
       gateway — the failure mode this repo exists for is ingest running inside
       the process it supervises, which crash-looped seven times in 3m34s on
       2026-09-07 while the loop kept ticking against a ledger that had stopped
       receiving signals.

       A LaunchAgent has no stdout consumer, so the move required more than a
       plist: this poller now delivers its own digest via a plain HTTP
       chat.postMessage (--post, see scripts/watchdog-poll.py's post_text()),
       never the gateway's live connection — the same property that makes the
       act-loop (com.jkrumm.warden-loop) safe to run independently. Its cron
       wrapper (watchdog-slack.py) is not a pure orphan: the UptimeKuma
       self-health heartbeat it carried on a clean run is ported into main()
       itself, fired only outside --dry-run. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__HOME__/SourceRoot/warden/.venv/bin/python3</string>
    <string>__HOME__/SourceRoot/warden/scripts/watchdog-poll.py</string>
    <string>--post</string>
  </array>
  <!-- 1800s = the */30 the cron job ran on. Unchanged deliberately. -->
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>1800</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/warden-poll.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/warden-poll.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
